   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_VQbrcqSMndgSwnWZ",
   "name": "Deriving Kinematic Equations of Motion",
   "definition": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Deriving kinematic equations of motion"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The kinematic equations of motion are a set of four equations which can describe any object moving with **constant** acceleration\n- They relate the five variables:\n\n  - *s* = **displacement**\n  - *u* = **initial velocity**\n  - *v* = **final velocity**\n  - *a* = **acceleration**\n  - *t* = **time interval**\n- It’s important to know where these equations come from and how they are derived:"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Deriving v = u + at"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/2.1.2-Deriving-vuat.png",
   "file": "assets/303b8c516cf1-2-1-2-deriving-vuat.png",
   "alt": "Deriving v=u+at, downloadable AS & A Level Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***A graph showing how the velocity of an object varies with time***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Deriving s = $\\frac{1}{2}$(u + v)t"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/2.1.2-Deriving-suvt-2.png",
   "file": "assets/7c63d929c534-2-1-2-deriving-suvt-2.png",
   "alt": "Deriving s=(u+v)t 2, downloadable AS & A Level Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***The average velocity is halfway between u and v***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Deriving s = ut + $\\frac{1}{2}$at<sup>2</sup>"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/2.1.2-Deriving-sut12at2.png",
   "file": "assets/67d39756fba0-2-1-2-deriving-sut12at2.png",
   "alt": "Deriving s=ut+12at2, downloadable AS & A Level Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***The two terms ut and ½at***<sup>***2***</sup>*** make up the area under the graph***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Deriving v<sup>2</sup> = u<sup>2</sup> + 2as"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/2.1.2-Deriving-v2u22as.png",
   "file": "assets/069f96335ede-2-1-2-deriving-v2u22as.png",
   "alt": "Deriving v2=u2+2as, downloadable AS & A Level Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***This final equation can be derived from two of the others***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Summary of the equations of motion"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/09/2.1.2-Summary-of-equations.png",
   "file": "assets/3aeaca3b3cd8-2-1-2-summary-of-equations.png",
   "alt": "Summary of equations, downloadable AS & A Level Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Summary of the four equations of uniformly accelerated motion***"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "Only $s=ut+\\frac{1}{2}at^{2}$ and $v^{2}=u^{2}+2as$ are given on your data sheet for your exam - make sure you remember **all** the equations of motions and their derivations."
  }
 ]
}